  "drivers": "Futures are lower for a second day as oil jumps: WTI is up about 4.8% to $92.5 and Brent about 4.7% to $105 after Axios reported the Pentagon told Central Command to finish preparations for resuming major combat operations in Iran, President Trump said he does not want an Iran deal, and tanker attacks in the Gulf and Strait of Hormuz continue. The 10-year yield is near 5.33% and the 30-year near 5.66%, close to multidecade highs, after Wednesday's FOMC minutes showed most officials still see one more hike by year-end as likely. Chips are weak despite TSMC's 51% quarterly revenue jump: SOX ETFs are off ~2% with Intel, STMicro and NXP (downgrade) leading. Single-stock news: PepsiCo beat but cut its core EPS growth outlook, Levi missed on revenue, argenx halted a Phase 3 trial, and Viatris agreed to buy Pacira. Fed Governor Waller speaks today on the policy path; ECB minutes are also out.",
